{"availability":"available","full":"lokutor-ai/ito","name":"ito","description":"Natural-sounding streaming text-to-speech for the ESP32-S3: 4.4 M params, 4.9 MB, no cloud, no NPU","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":5,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T14:45:34Z","updated":"2026-10-02T22:53:02Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lokutor-ai.github.io/ito/","topics":["edge-ai","embedded","esp32","esp32-s3","microcontroller","speech-synthesis","streaming","text-to-speech","tinyml","tts"],"demo":"https://lokutor-ai.github.io/ito/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.845Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.845Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.845Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.845Z","stars":5,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ito is English text-to-speech that runs entirely on an ESP32-S3 (240 MHz dual-core Xtensa LX7, 8 MB PSRAM, 16 MB flash), with no cloud and no neural accelerator. It streams: audio starts after a short first chunk (25 ms) is ready, and the work before it does not grow with the sentence length. The voice is distilled from a large open TTS model into 4.4 M parameters. Built by Lokutor, the makers of Oído (speech recognition on the same chip).","Status (3 October 2026). The on-chip engine is verified on a laptop and in Espressif's QEMU emulator: the firmware's audio is bit-identical to the host build of the engine, and every sample in samples/ is that engine's exact output. Nothing has run on a physical board yet. Time to first audio and real-time factor are estimated from exact instruction counts (QEMU) and an assumed PSRAM bandwidth. Real-time playback is not established on silicon: the optimistic and central estimates are faster than real time (RTF 0.53–0.54 and 0.77–0.80) and the pessimistic one is still slower (1.18–1.27). The…","Licensing in one line. The code is GPLv3; the voice model that makes it talk is non-commercial (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 + terms). Hobby, research and education use is welcome. For anything commercial, or if you are a small team that wants to build with it, talk to us: we like collaborating."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9bd0f2ca2df0dbeb2e3f5a3639173af6b19e727850eb3fd5f43eaab45209ce37","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:53.289Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ito is English text-to-speech that runs entirely on an ESP32-S3 (240 MHz dual-core Xtensa LX7, 8 MB PSRAM, 16 MB flash), with no cloud and no neural accelerator. It streams: audio starts after a short first chunk (25 ms) is ready, and the work before it does not grow with the sentence length. The voice is distilled from a large open TTS model into 4.4 M parameters. Built by Lokutor, the makers of Oído (speech recognition on the same chip).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Open it, accept the terms (free for research, education and personal projects), then log in on your machine:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9bd0f2ca2df0dbeb2e3f5a3639173af6b19e727850eb3fd5f43eaab45209ce37","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:53.289Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T22:53:02Z","overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:45.380Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:53.290Z","hash":"9bd0f2ca2df0dbeb2e3f5a3639173af6b19e727850eb3fd5f43eaab45209ce37","originalBytes":18891,"storedBytes":18891,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["ito","voice","chip","firs